From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:25:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?duck-brain=20P19:=20the=20P5=20set=20of=2022.10?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20roller=20networks,=20the=20brake,=20standing=20o?=
 =?UTF-8?q?n=20rollers?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Alex's set of 22.10 replaces every policy: on legs the walk v2, the
stand-up and FallSafe; on rollers the ride, the brake and the roller
stand-up, all at P 5 / D 0 with a runtime manifest each (P17).

- The roller networks' metadata lists the skates' free wheels among the
  joints (`passive_LF_wheel`, ...): they are dropped, with their
  `default_joint_pos` entries, before the 14 are checked.
- On rollers (`mode = "roller"`, Controller::on_rollers), Alex's rule of
  22.10: a commanded speed rides; a stop brakes only a robot that was
  rolling — the `brake` skill for its `duration`, cmd[0] = +/-0.3 by the
  sign of the speed — then the ride stands on a zero command, as it does
  for a robot that was not rolling. Nothing measures rolling speed (the
  wheels are free, the contact odometry is for feet), so the speed is the
  one the ride was following when the stop came. A fall clears it. The
  brake does not start by hand. The fall chain runs as on legs — ride ->
  FallSafe -> the standing network (the roller stand-up) -> ride — with
  standing measured to the tyres and above 127 mm.
- duck_control::stance has both models now, from the runtime model of
  Alex's redrawn duck (duck-brain model/robot_walk.xml, robot_rollers.xml):
  soles on legs, tyres (swept round their free axles) on rollers, checked
  against MuJoCo (0.19 / 0.26 mm); the P5 HOME, trunk exactly upright,
  stands at 116.4 / 140.0 mm.
- The tests on networks that are gone (the ride v2 with its swizzle
  clock, Fish, the stride, the 32/40 stand-up) are replaced by tests on
  the six: each loads with its manifest, 61 in / 14 out; the roller
  brake and fall chain; a set with a manifest-less network refused.
